    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0550" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1042: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-07T12:00:00-04:30">February 7,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Department’s telegram 1, February 6, 6 p.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d472-f1"/>
                    Message to Peruvian Government delivered through Venezuelan Legation in Lima
                    supported Brazilian proposal and American note. No instructions were given to
                    mention Kellogg Pact.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d472-f1" n="3" xml:id="d472-f1-content">
                <p>It read “Your No. 2, February 3, 5 p.m. Was Venezuelan telegram to Peru based on
                    Kellogg Pact? This is important.” (721.23/994)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
